Every application you build relies on these fundamental pillars....

🔰 Compute

 Servers – Traditional compute machines hosting your app.
 Containers – Lightweight, portable environments (Docker, K8s).
 Serverless – Run code without managing servers (AWS Lambda).
 FaaS – Function as a Service for event-triggered logic.
 PaaS – Platform to deploy apps without infrastructure headache.

 🔰 Architecture Patterns

 Monolith – All-in-one codebase, tightly coupled.
 Microservices – Split app into independent, loosely coupled services.
 Event-driven – Services communicate via events, not direct calls.
 Serverless – Entire architecture built on managed services.

 🔰 Networking

 DNS – Maps domain names to IP addresses.
 Load Balancers – Distribute traffic across multiple servers.
 CDNs – Cache and serve content closer to users.
 VPNs – Secure private access to a network.
 Firewalls – Filter incoming and outgoing traffic.
 NAT – Translate private IPs to public and vice versa.
 Gateways – Entry/exit point to a network.
 Proxies – Intermediate server for requests.
 Routers – Direct packets across networks.

🔰 Storage

 Database – Store structured data (SQL/NoSQL).
 Object Storage – Store unstructured data like images/videos.
 Block Storage – Raw volume-based storage for VMs.
 File Systems – Organize and manage files.
 Caching – Store frequently accessed data in-memory (Redis, Memcached).

🔰  Communication

 APIs – Define how software components interact.
 Message Queue – Buffer messages between producer and consumer.
 WebSocket – Real-time full-duplex communication.
 Pub/Sub – Publishers push messages; subscribers listen.
 RPC – Remote call to another service as if it's local.
 Service Mesh – Manage service-to-service communication.

 🔰 Security

 Authentication – Proving who you are.
 Authorization – Deciding what you're allowed to do.
 Encryption – Securing data at rest and in transit.
 Security Protocols – SSL/TLS, HTTPS, OAuth etc.
 WAF – Protects apps from common attacks.
 IDS – Detects unauthorized access or anomalies.

🔰 Observability

 Monitoring – Alerting on infrastructure/app health.
 Logging – Recording system and application events.
 Tracing – Following request flow across services.
 Metrics – Quantitative data like CPU, latency, throughput.
 APM – Application Performance Monitoring tools for deep insights.

 🔰 Scalability & Resilience

 Horizontal Scaling – Add more machines.
 Vertical Scaling – Add more resources to a single machine.
 Sharding – Split data across multiple databases.
 Redundancy – Duplicate systems for reliability.
 Fault Tolerance – System works even if parts fail.
 Disaster Recovery – Restore service after catastrophic failure.
